<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/TestFlight-App-Store.jpeg" alt="" width="160" height="90" class="alignleft size-full wp-image-1062490" />As <a href="https://x.com/viticci/status/2095667534871634111">noted</a> by <em>MacStories</em> editor-in-chief Federico Viticci, TestFlight now shows recent betas by default again for all users.<br/>
<br/>
In July, Apple updated TestFlight with a search field for quickly finding apps that you are beta testing, but some users started to see their apps presented in alphabetical order. It is not entirely clear if this was a bug or an intentional change, but many users did not like it, and TestFlight version 4.3.1 reverses course. The update with the fix is <a href="https://apps.apple.com/us/app/testflight/id899247664">available in the App Store</a> now. The search field remains.<div class="linkback">Tag: <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/testflight/">TestFlight</a></div><br/>This article, &quot;<a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/04/apple-just-fixed-testflight/">Apple Just Fixed TestFlight</a>&quot; first appeared on <a href="https://www.macrumors.com">MacRumors.com</a><br/><br/><a href="https://forums.macrumors.com/threads/apple-just-fixed-testflight.2488476/">Discuss this article</a> in our forums<br/><br/>